Falsifies `network_time_protocol::verification::a_consistent_exchange_is_accepted`.

The defect: the stratum check refuses `MAXIMUM_STRATUM` itself, `>=` where the rule is `>`. It
reads as a tidy bound, since 16 is the unsynchronised stratum and 15 sits right under it.

Expected to fail: the harness's `expect("a consistent exchange is refused")`, on a stratum of 15,
the farthest a synchronised server may be from a reference clock.

--- a/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs
@@ -724,7 +724,7 @@
         if p.is_kiss_of_death() {
             return Err(Reject::KissOfDeath(p.reference_id));
         }
-        if p.stratum > MAXIMUM_STRATUM {
+        if p.stratum >= MAXIMUM_STRATUM {
             return Err(Reject::Stratum(p.stratum));
         }
         if p.leap == leap::UNSYNCHRONISED {
